{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"So I have talked to a buddy of mine that codes some basic discord bots for another server I am on.  If it works, it will have 2 main functions:\n1) at 4 specified times of day, every day, it will post custom messages into specified channels.\nWhat this means is: at say midnight, 6am, noon, 6pm you could have your burrough have a custom note (imagine at 6pm it says \"What A Horrible Night To Have A Curse\" and at 6am it could say \"The morning sun has vanquished the horrible night.\" for example)\n\nthis can add a bit of atmosphere to your burrough, but might also be seen as spammy, so maybe we jsut have 1 channel that will let people know its midnight, dawn, noon, and dusk.\n\nthe cooler and more important feature is 2) at those same times, it also checks channels for date/time and announces on those channels what news you have.\n\nSo this means, (actual formatting is not determined yet) I could say on \"7/12/2021 at morning in # hampstead-streets: Rumors of people vanishing at night are spreading.\"\n\"7/12/2021 at evening in # hampstead-streets: @ everyone Aper Filos has offered his homestead for people to meet at to seek out the missing people. (player note: at 8pm, roughly 2 hours from now, meet at # the-ricter-homestead for tonights event).\n\nIn addition, a fog rolls in.  If you are not sure what the fog does, read the document at world-anvil-link-here\"\n\nobviously with at's and # and other discord properly working... i just didn't want to ping or link in this post.  Anyway, Ill keep you all up to date on this bots status, and what the formatting will need to look like... but hopefully it becomes a way for us to deliver information for the game even if we are currently offline, allowing players to talk/discuss that day's events.","created_at":"2021-02-05T15:03:53.695000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"807265249295859762","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
